WEBVTT

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:41.660
In ancient times, when the ancestor of the Queen descended from Ephon Noha to Tahai Aze, 　

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:46.960
the people met the Founding King, Je, who was tall and had golden eyes.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.170
It was the holy God Himself.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:57.390
So many thousands of days and nights later,

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:01.680
since the capital governed by the Queen does not have an army,

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.980
it is now currently protected by the Grand Duke,

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:07.900
who possesses an army specializing in Touda, and technically governs the quarters on the other side of the mountains.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:15.740
The Grand Duke's lionhearted soldiers fight the invasion from the neighboring country by using the strength of the Touda.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:25.750
The Touda used by the Grand Duke's army are raised in Ake Village, away from the capital and the battlefield.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.090
Erin-chan!  Are you all right?

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:18.800
Saju!  What are you doing?

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:23.010
Erin-chan's in trouble!  Don't just watch!  Help me!

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.310
Oh, great.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.810
Ready... pull!

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:36.820
Ouch...

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.070
What got you in there, Erin?

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:43.830
A goat popped its head out over me, so I was startled.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:52.840
Erin-chan?

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:56.920
It's capracide.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.340
What's wrong?

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.600
It's capracide.  We have to get rid of them.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.310
It'd be really bad if the goats ate these!

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.850
They'd die from poisoning!

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:10.440
Chok, go let the people in the village know about this!

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:11.690
Okay!

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:22.660
Soyon the Beastinarian

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:30.580
Erin-chan.  Looks like we're done over here.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:31.620
Okay.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:36.170
But how did capracide grow at a place like this?

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.550
What could that be?

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:42.090
It's too early for the chronicle bell.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.810
There's a Touda at the village's entrance!

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:48.600
A Touda?

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.240
Who is he?

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:08.410
He must be a soldier from two quarters away.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:09.910
How can you tell?

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:16.000
The crest etched onto the Touda's hard scale is different from ours, right?

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.340
You're right.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:21.630
Dad said that's how you can tell the difference.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:23.800
Wow, really?

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:31.770
He is Hasson-dono, the Chief of Ake.

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:35.230
I'm Wadan, a beastinarian.

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:37.360
I'm Tairan from the Togi quarter.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:38.730
I'm a Touda rider.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:41.690
I came all the way here to ask a favor of you.

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:45.660
Why would you bring a Touda from Togi all the way to Ake?

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:50.290
On the battlefield, I was told that there's a good doctor in this village.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:51.660
Are you the one?

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:56.380
Yeah, it's true that I'm a good doctor.

00:05:57.130 --> 00:06:00.880
At a glance, that Touda does not seem to have any external injuries.

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:02.420
Is it sick?

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:05.840
This Touda is like my own arm.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:12.520
We've fought through many battles together, but it quit eating the moment we returned home.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.480
Won't eat, you say?

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:16.560
At this rate, it'll starve to death.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.480
I want you to save it.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.570
What do you usually feed it?

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:21.980
Goat meat.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.820
No different than us.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:24.650
Hey!

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:30.370
Due to the village code, we can't disclose any more details.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:35.460
Tairan-dono, every Touda is a treasure of its village.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:39.250
Even at the moment of death, its fate is either to die at the village where it was born or on the battlefield.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.340
Have you forgotten that?

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.340
I've received the Grand Duke's permission.

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:46.430
The Grand Duke?

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:50.850
If the Grand Duke permits it, then I guess we don't have a choice.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:52.930
Thank you very much.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:54.020
Then, let's-

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:55.140
Bring Soyon here.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.900
Soyon?

00:06:58.350 --> 00:06:59.400
That's right.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:02.690
Okay.

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:05.780
He called for Soyon Oba-san.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:06.860
Yeah.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:14.540
An Arryo?  Not to mention a female beastinarian?

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:17.670
That woman's no longer of the Mist People.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:24.670
She's the wife of my deceased son, a member of this village, and is the best beastinarian here.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:28.260
I see.  So she doesn't possess any shady spells?

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:37.180
I can't say anything definite without monitoring it for a while.

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:41.730
I'll formulate some benetrophic water, but I can't guarantee its recovery.

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:44.440
I came prepared, even for the worst.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:45.690
Please take care of it.

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:50.700
Chief, since this is a foreign Touda, we can't put it in one of our ponds.  What should we do?

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:52.240
Let's see...

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.370
In that case, there's a perfect pond to use.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.450
The pond at my workshop.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.670
Then let's take care of it there for a while.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.290
I'm indebted to you.

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:11.260
It won't eat at all.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:12.340
No...

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:15.970
Hey, you guys!

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:18.270
Who allowed you to come here?!

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:23.610
Ah, I bet that Mist woman sent you here, didn't she?

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:27.280
No.  My mother has nothing to do with this.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:30.570
Yeah!  I'm the one who asked to go see it!

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:32.070
How can I be sure about that?

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:36.950
I hear Mist People travel from place to place in order to steal secrets.

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:40.580
You never know what a woman that came from such a place would do.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.330
Mother would never do such a thing!

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.210
Yeah?

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:45.920
Let's go, Erin-chan!

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:46.960
Yeah.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:20.910
Come on in.

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.880
Capital-sect-publication?

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:30.550
It's a publication written by the reverend of the capital's sect.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:33.380
There are facts about herbs written in this.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.970
But this book is about poison.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:38.470
It might be a bit too soon for you to read it.

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:40.720
I'm already ten, you know.

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:43.730
Grandfather told me that I could go to the ponds, too.

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:47.980
That's because you snuck into the ponds.

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:54.610
I asked him to allow it, by promising to keep you within my range of sight.

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:59.790
I'm sure I'll be able to take care of Touda when I grow up.

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.290
Are Touda scary to you?

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:04.750
N-No, they're not.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:10.630
If you think Touda are scary, then you can become a good doctor.

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:32.860
Erin-chan.  These keep coming up no matter how much we pull them out.

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:36.740
We have to pull them out before the flowers bloom, or else the seeds will spread,

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:39.950
and if the roots remain in the ground, we'll have to uproot them again.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:42.120
So much work!

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:44.410
Stop complaining, Saju.

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:45.660
It's your job.

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:50.000
You're lucky, Onee-chan, since you're going to get married soon.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:57.890
You're right.  Once I'm gone, work hard with Erin-chan, all right?

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:03.220
She's been acting strangely recently.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:05.680
Let's finish this up.

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:08.940
It's Tairan-san.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:11.690
Where could he be headed to?

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:14.490
He has a spear, so...

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:16.280
Maybe to practice with his spear?

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:18.740
I'm going to go take a look!

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:21.030
I'll go, too!

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:58.990
Wow!

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:10.710
At the battlefield, I have to catch fresh food for my Touda and me on the spot,

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:14.250
so I picked up that little trick from who-knows-where.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:18.470
You were riding that Touda on the battlefield, right?

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:20.550
Are Touda strong?

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:24.760
It's said that a Touda can eat a hundred horses, right?

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:26.560
The phrase says it all.

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:28.020
They're that strong?

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:33.730
This country is at peace thanks to the protection provided by Touda.

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:40.610
And, amongst them, Touda referred to as Kiba, which are allowed to be ridden only by the chosen ones of the Grand Duke,

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:45.160
are extra large and possess tougher bodies and fangs.

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:48.410
There's one in this village too, right?

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:51.870
Yes.  My mother's taking care of it.

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:57.630
Only the best are allowed to take care of Kiba.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:03.140
If your mother's the one looking after it, then my Touda may be cured, too.

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:07.060
Thank you.

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:08.390
Eh?  Ah...

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:09.600
You're welcome.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:12.560
I see.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:17.690
I can tell what your mother's like by looking at you.

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:21.990
You can tell what my mother's like by looking at me?

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:25.070
Yes.  It's often said that children are their parents' mirror.

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:31.620
Seeing how polite you are, she must be a strict person, even to herself.

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:35.040
Tairan-sama!

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:36.960
Is the Touda cured?

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:39.460
No!  It suddenly started shivering!

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:40.090
What?

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:42.010
Please come right away!

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:47.010
Wait for me!

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.820
It's poisoned.

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:01.320
What did you feed it?

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:04.070
Only benetrophic water as medicine.

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:07.530
It's similar to the symptoms from capracide poisoning.

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:10.240
I didn't add any such thing.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:13.500
Tairan-sama.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.000
We can't think optimistically anymore.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:23.170
If it had the strength of a normal Touda, I think it might survive.

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:27.840
But, first and foremost, this Touda has to eat something.

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:30.310
Erin-chan, I said wait.

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:35.810
Get away!

00:15:03.050 --> 00:15:05.380
What just happened?

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:14.850
Tell me your thoughts.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:19.350
It must have been poisoned through benetrophic water.

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:21.310
"Poisoned?"

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:27.280
Providing benetrophic water to a healthy Touda will strengthen its body,

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:30.070
but it was likely too strong for a weakened Touda.

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:33.410
You're saying that the potency of the benetrophic water was too great and it went berserk?

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:37.580
I can't say anything certain without further research.

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:39.500
Then go do your research.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:44.590
But don't forget that you'll be blamed if that Touda dies.

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:47.050
That's the code among those who deal with Touda.

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:48.470
Yes.

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:16.870
Thank you, Erin.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.970
I don't see any flowers.

00:16:37.020 --> 00:16:42.480
I was wondering if it was some rat, but look, it's a daughter of the Mist People.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:43.940
Tairan-san!

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:51.320
I see.  So you think it was capracide that made my Touda go berserk.

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:56.580
Yes.  In my mother's book, it said that it also makes goats go berserk and die.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:00.040
Oh, no.  Don't worry about it.

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:04.750
But something's strange.

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:09.710
If capracide was the cause, then it should have gone berserk sooner.

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:12.930
Erin-chan!

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:14.510
Oh, Tairan-san's here.

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:16.640
Can you show us your fishing again?

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:24.270
Sure thing.  My Touda won't get better even if I sit here.

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:29.480
I guess I'll catch some fish for it to eat, believing that it'll get better.

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:35.490
That's it!

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:38.830
It's the fish!

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:42.120
Mom!

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:44.080
Erin.  What's wrong?

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:47.090
These.

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:52.050
Waterfall mountain trout?

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:53.340
Watch this.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.230
I guess not.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:12.280
Not yet.

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:15.660
Erin!

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:28.630
Don't worry.  Eat this.

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:40.510
Tairan-san, now!

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:42.140
I'm on it!

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:45.890
There.

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:46.730
There.

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:48.360
Erin...

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:52.820
I heard that Tairan-san's Touda ate fish all the time.

00:18:52.820 --> 00:18:54.440
Fish... all the time?

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:59.320
So that's why it doesn't eat the goat meat.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:10.460
But I still don't understand why it showed symptoms of capracide poisoning.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:13.670
Maybe Wadan-san made a mistake.

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:18.260
Erin.  Wadan-san is a beastinarian just like me.

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:22.260
He knows well what's good and what's not.

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:23.930
You mustn't talk bad about others.

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:26.430
I'm sorry.

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:33.480
I brought the ingredients from the preparation shack and blended them here,

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:34.820
but I got the same result.

00:19:49.170 --> 00:19:50.250
Go get some water.

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:51.290
Yes.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:58.010
There we go.

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:04.600
Chok, don't!

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:11.860
What was that about, all of a sudden?

00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:12.900
I knew it.

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:14.190
Knew what?

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:15.530
Mom!

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:17.490
What is it?

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:21.910
It's capracide.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:29.500
The capracide's poison dissolved in water was the cause of the Touda going berserk.

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:35.800
After the capracide was removed and the water was refilled,

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:41.300
the Touda started to drink benetrophic water.

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:46.260
I'm glad for you that it became completely healthy again.

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:48.100
Thank you very much.

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:50.350
I will surely repay this debt one day.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:52.560
We don't need anything.

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:56.780
All we ask you to do is fight on the battlefield for the sake of this country.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:00.280
Where might Soyon-dono be?

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:04.530
She must be excusing herself from attending.

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:05.990
I see.

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:11.210
Well, Soyon-dono was amazing, but seeing how the girl noticed about the fish and the capracide,

00:21:11.210 --> 00:21:13.880
she has a great successor.

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:25.640
You didn't need to go send him off?

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:27.890
You didn't go, either.

00:21:28.310 --> 00:21:29.850
I'm amazed that you noticed.

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:32.310
Noticed that you're here?

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:35.560
I'm talking about the fish and the capracide.

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:48.280
Do you want to give it a try?

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:49.910
I can?!

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:05.760
Erin.  If you really want to become a Touda doctor, then I will teach you properly.

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:07.850
Okay!

00:22:09.060 --> 00:22:11.020
Touda are scary creatures.

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:19.020
But Erin was learning that Touda are also animals, through polishing its body.

00:22:19.480 --> 00:22:26.820
She strongly wishes to become a Touda doctor like her mother.

00:24:02.090 --> 00:24:04.210
A Touda is a tool of war.

00:24:04.550 --> 00:24:07.630
Ake Village is a village composed of Touda breeders who raise them.

00:24:08.550 --> 00:24:14.640
Training for Kiba which are kept
for the Grand Duke takes place,

00:24:14.640 --> 00:24:19.520
and Erin unexpectedly sees the Touda's alternate face from the battlefield.

00:24:20.770 --> 00:24:24.480
Kemono no Souja Erin.  The Fighting Beast.

00:24:25.030 --> 00:24:30.030
The Fighting Beast
